IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sea-formulas`

-- Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 -- worked cases for the amounts computed from the formulas sidecar
-- (C2004A04525.formulas.md), from the seat of the injured seafarer.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand
-- from the formulas and the deposited text (C2025C00116), never copied from the encoding's output; the working is in the
-- comment above each case. No scenario life raised this Act; every case is HYPOTHETICAL. The indexed amounts used are
-- the compilation's printed figures standing in for those in force; the AWOTE ($2,000) and the rate per kilometre ($0.80)
-- are made-up figures.
--
-- Mia (HYPOTHETICAL), an able seafarer on a prescribed ship in interstate trade, on a weekly salary of $2,000.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 13 -- normal weekly earnings`

-- The arguments: weekly salary; percentage increase under s 13(5); percentage change under s 13(6).
-- Mia's weekly salary under her contract, nothing since: 2,000.
#ASSERT `my normal weekly earnings under s 13` 2000 0 0 EQUALS 2000
-- She would have moved up an increment of 5%: 2,000 × 1.05 = 2,100.
#ASSERT `my normal weekly earnings under s 13` 2000 5 0 EQUALS 2100
-- And the class's award rate was then cut by 2%: 2,100 × 0.98 = 2,058.
#ASSERT `my normal weekly earnings under s 13` 2000 5 -2 EQUALS 2058

§§ `s 28(6A) -- travel to treatment`

-- The arguments: compensable; public transport or ambulance; reasonably required; fares; car kilometres; rate per kilometre.
-- 120.9 km there and back by car at $0.80: whole kilometres, 120 × 0.80 = 96.
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment under the Seafarers Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 120.9 0.8 EQUALS 96
-- 40 km by car: not over 50 km (s 28(7)(b)), nothing.
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment under the Seafarers Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 40 0.8 EQUALS 0
-- By ambulance, which the injury reasonably required, costing $45.50: the expenditure, 45.50 (s 28(6A)(a)).
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment under the Seafarers Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE 45.5 0 0.8 EQUALS 45.5
-- By bus when the injury did not require it: nothing (s 28(7)(a)).
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment under the Seafarers Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE 12 0 0.8 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 31 -- the weekly amount in dollars`

-- The arguments: incapacitated; earlier weeks towards 45; NWE; able to earn in suitable employment; hours employed; normal
-- weekly hours; worked as a seafarer; AWOTE; $254.46; $62.99; $31.50; a prescribed person dependent; prescribed children;
-- pension age; injured within a year of it; weeks compensated; in prison.
-- Week 11 after she was put ashore, unable to work: 2,000 − 0 = 2,000 (s 31(2)).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 10 2000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 2000
-- Week 11, able to earn $800 ashore in suitable employment: 2,000 − 800 = 1,200.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 10 2000 800 19 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 1200
-- Week 45 (44 before it), the last of the first 45: still s 31(2), 2,000.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 44 2000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 2000
-- A master on $5,000 a week in the first 45 weeks: the s 31(7) cap reaches only s 31(5) amounts, so 5,000.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 10 5000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 5000
-- Able to earn $2,500, more than her normal weekly earnings: negative, read as nil.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 10 2000 2500 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 0
-- A low earner (NWE $400, able to earn $100) in the first 45 weeks: 400 − 100 = 300, with no minimum earnings.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 10 400 100 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 300
-- The same after 45 weeks: 75% × 400 − 100 = 200, raised to min(254.46 + 62.99 + 2 × 31.50 = 380.45, 90% × 400 = 360) = 360
-- (the figure sea-cases-employee.l4 asserts through the band question; this is the dollar question agreeing).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 50 400 100 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 360
-- After 45 weeks, not working, NWE 2,000: 75% = 1,500.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 50 2000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 1500
-- Pension age reached (s 38(1)), or not incapacitated: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` TRUE 10 2000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week in dollars` FALSE 10 2000 0 0 38 FALSE 2000 254.46 62.99 31.50 TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 0

§§ `s 41 -- non-economic loss`

-- The arguments: finger, toe, taste or smell; degree of permanent impairment; degree of non-economic loss; $18,895.98 in force.
-- 20% impairment, 30% non-economic loss: 18,895.98 × 20% = 3,779.196, plus 18,895.98 × 30% = 5,668.794: 9,447.99.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss under the Seafarers Act` FALSE 20 30 18895.98 EQUALS 9447.99
-- 9% impairment: below the s 39(7) threshold, no s 39 compensation, none under s 41.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss under the Seafarers Act` FALSE 9 30 18895.98 EQUALS 0
-- The loss of a toe at 5% (no threshold, s 39(8)), non-economic loss 10%: 944.799 + 1,889.598 = 2,834.397.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss under the Seafarers Act` TRUE 5 10 18895.98 EQUALS 2834.397

§§ `ss 23, 23A -- indexation`

-- The arguments: later index number; earlier index number.
-- 140 / 135 = 1.03703...: 1.037. 103.75 / 100 = 1.0375, 4th place 5: 1.038. 103.74 / 100: 1.037.
#ASSERT `the Seafarers Act indexation factor` 140 135 EQUALS 1.037
#ASSERT `the Seafarers Act indexation factor` 103.75 100 EQUALS 1.038
#ASSERT `the Seafarers Act indexation factor` 103.74 100 EQUALS 1.037
-- The arguments: index; amount before; December quarter index before the year; the one a year earlier.
-- $254.46 (s 31(9)) on a CPI factor of 1.037: 254.46 + 254.46 × 0.037 (9.41502) = 263.87502.
#ASSERT `the Seafarers Act amount after a year's indexation` `the Consumer Price Index (s 23: the amounts in ss 30(2), 31(9) to (11), 39(9), 41(2), 43(2), (4), 44(1))` 254.46 140 135 EQUALS 263.87502
-- $412,000 (s 29(3)) on WPI 104.2 over 100 = 1.042: 429,304.
#ASSERT `the Seafarers Act amount after a year's indexation` `the Wage Price Index (s 23A: the amounts in s 29(3) to (5))` 412000 104.2 100 EQUALS 429304
-- A WPI that fell, 99 over 100: no substitution.
#ASSERT `the Seafarers Act amount after a year's indexation` `the Wage Price Index (s 23A: the amounts in s 29(3) to (5))` 412000 99 100 EQUALS 412000
